    "problem_statement": "EncloseAnsiText function produces incorrect ANSI escape sequence enclosure\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `EncloseAnsiText` function in `terminal.py` is not properly enclosing ANSI/SGR escape sequences. The function appears to be swapping the start and end markers, resulting in incorrect output.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom textfsm import terminal\n\n# Test with ANSI escape sequences\nansi_text = '\\x1b[5;32;44mansi\\x1b[0m length'\nresult = terminal.EncloseAnsiText(ansi_text)\nprint(\"Result:\", repr(result))\nprint(\"Expected:\", repr('\\x01\\x1b[5;32;44m\\x02ansi\\x01\\x1b[0m\\x02 length'))\n```\n\nThe function should enclose ANSI escape sequences with `\\x01` (ANSI_START) at the beginning and `\\x02` (ANSI_END) at the end, but it's currently doing the opposite."
